        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"writing-better-code-using-functions-tests\">Writing Better Code Using <strong>Functions</strong> &amp; <strong>Tests</strong></h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Faizan Imran</li>\n<li>Data Science Intern - <strong>Modeling Team</strong> - Department of Finance (2026)</li>\n<li>Current grad student at UChicago - majors: <strong>Computer Science &amp; Public Policy</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"agenda\">Agenda:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What are functions?<ul>\n<li>Types of functions<ul>\n<li>Pure Functions</li>\n<li>Impure Functions</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Why write functions at all?</li>\n<li>When to write functions?</li>\n<li>Database Connection - Case Study</li>\n<li>How functions facilitate testing</li>\n<li>Unit Testing</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "8d4660be927016eaccc09bf3edcde981",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<marimo-callout-output data-html='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eSome of us might remember functions from Maths - they are formally defined as: &#92;u003cem&#92;u003e&#92;&quot;A function from a set X to a set Y assigns to each element of X exactly one element of Y&#92;&quot;&#92;u003c/em&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;n&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eThe same can logic can be applied to computer functions! A function can be thought of as a &#92;&quot;reusable block of code that performs &#92;u003cstrong&#92;u003ea specific task&#92;u003c/strong&#92;u003e&#92;&quot;.&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;n&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eIt helps to think of functions as a machine that receives as input and processes that input in some predetermined way and returns some output.&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;' data-kind='&quot;info&quot;' data-title='&quot;What is a function?&quot;'></marimo-callout-output>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "fc77cd4c895943a31fc2be7a637a2c30",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"why-functions\">Why Functions?</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Functions are a great way to streamline work as Data Scientists/Analysts/Engineers - writing functions allows us to name processes, avoid redundancies and work on our organizational/team specific code base incrementally.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Some immediately useful features of writing code in functions are<sup id=\"fnref:676-1\"><a class=\"footnote-ref\" href=\"#fn:676-1\">1</a></sup><sup id=\"fnref:676-2\"><a class=\"footnote-ref\" href=\"#fn:676-2\">2</a></sup>:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Modularity</strong>: Functions help remove redundancies and improve efficiency by making code modular.</li>\n<li><strong>Memory</strong>: Function names are easy to remember and communicate. And the variable/objects defined inside of functions are not stored in memory aftear the function runs - saving computer memory!</li>\n<li><strong>Maintainability</strong>: Functions are easy to update; to make changes we would need to only update the code in one place. This makes our codebase much more easier to maintain and expand in the long run.</li>\n<li><strong>Tests &amp; Checks</strong>: We can explicitly handle issues and edge cases when writing functions and they also make it much easier to write tests.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"footnote\">\n<hr />\n<ol>\n<li id=\"fn:676-1\"><a href=\"https://r4ds.hadley.nz/functions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Hadley Wickham - R for Data Science</a>&#160;<a class=\"footnote-backref\" href=\"#fnref:676-1\" title=\"Jump back to footnote 1 in the text\">&#8617;</a></li>\n<li id=\"fn:676-2\"><a href=\"https://www.pyopensci.org/lessons/write-better-code/optimize-code/about-python-functions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Why Write Functions?</a>&#160;<a class=\"footnote-backref\" href=\"#fnref:676-2\" title=\"Jump back to footnote 2 in the text\">&#8617;</a></li>\n</ol>\n</div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lEQa",
