    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "8e23bff210fa80f6882ac73be331e42f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"most-of-us-already-use-functions-all-the-time\">Most of us already use functions all the time!</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Both Python &amp; R have tons of <strong>built-in functions</strong> that we use all the time.\nOn top of that, both languages give us access to <strong>libraries/packages</strong>, where\nsomeone else already wrote a bunch of functions and published them for us to use!</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Here are some common built-in functions in Python:</span></span><marimo-ui-element object-id='Kclp-0' random-id='eb105332-a0d1-ad0a-0f2a-61c6ea2b561a'><marimo-tabs data-initial-value='&quot;&quot;' data-label='null' data-tabs='[&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003eprint()&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;,&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003esum()&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;,&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003elist()&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;]' data-orientation='&quot;horizontal&quot;'><div data-kind='tab'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Hello!\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<code>print()</code> shows text on the screen.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Fun fact: The <em>print()</em> function doesn't actually <em>return</em> anything, so if we store it's output in an object it will just be <code>None</code>.</span></span></div><div data-kind='tab'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nb\">sum</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<code>sum()</code> add things up.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Returns:</strong> <code>14</code></span></span></div><div data-kind='tab'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nb\">list</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"hello\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<code>list()</code> turns things into a list. A word becomes a list of its letters!</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Returns:</strong> <code>['h', 'e', 'l', 'l', 'o']</code></span></span></div></marimo-tabs></marimo-ui-element><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<span class=\"paragraph\">When we install a library like Pandas and import it in our code it comes with a lot of functions that it's creators built for our use, for example:\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pandas</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pd</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">df</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">pd</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">DataFrame</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">df</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isna</span><span class=\"p\">()</span> <span class=\"c1\"># Detect missing values for an array-like object.</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">df</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unique</span><span class=\"p\">()</span> <span class=\"c1\"># Return unique values based on a hash table.</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">df</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pivot</span><span class=\"p\">()</span> <span class=\"c1\"># Return reshaped DataFrame organized by given index / column values.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\nand many many more. These functions do task that most of us working with data need to do. Simply importing a library that has functions that perform tasks we need to do make our life much easier!</span>\n<hr />\n<h3 id=\"combining-functions-into-a-package\">Combining Functions into a Package</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Once we get comfortable with writing and managing our own functions we can also bundle them up in a package and publish them for others to use. My team at DOF did just that with the package <a href=\"https://github.com/nycdepartmentoffinance/assessNYC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">AssessNYC</a>. This package contains a bunch of functions that helps our team do all sorts of modelling/EDA work and it also speaks to the value of investing in functions early in local government because our workflows require (for the most part) having a base set of utilities/tasks that the Data Scientists/Engineers work on to improve and expand on over time!</span></span></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "c06f26af9f927c2e5fe57b0b46974c6a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"when-to-write-functions\">When to Write Functions</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A good rule of thumb to have when considering writing functions is to ask whether the piece of code that we have would need to copy/paste some lines of code while changing nothing or changing very little of the original structure.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "d2d8d6ae78c60f02a14318e101c4bc2e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h4 id=\"example-2\">Example 2:</h4>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">While at DOF our team was accessing data by connecting to a database and since the database connection was a central part of everyone's work almost all the scripts that everyone was writing had 8-10 lines of code that established the database connection.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">So I wrote a function that built the connection for them! Instead of manually writing 10 lines of code in every script this function allowed a single line access.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "b2e69ea1b54eec21fd96b94f095f845d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">connect_db</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    This function takes in the name of the database and establishes a connection</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    with that database.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    Input:</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    - db_name: (str) the name of the database to connect to</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    Returns:</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    - A pyodbc.Connection object which we can use to query our database</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    \"\"\"</span>\n\n    <span class=\"c1\"># the following line just loads in the .Renviron file that contains sensitive information</span>\n    <span class=\"c1\"># like passwords needed to connect to the database</span>\n\n    <span class=\"n\">load_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">find_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"C:/Users/</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getlogin</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">/.Renviron\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n\n    <span class=\"n\">connection_args</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Driver={Oracle in OraClient19Home1};\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DBQ=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_path'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DATABASE=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_schema'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"UID=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_username'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"PWD=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_password'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"s2\">\"Trusted_Connection=no;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"s2\">\"Port=1433\"</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">]</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">connection_string</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">join</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">connection_args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">pyodbc</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">connect</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">connection_string</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "iLit",
      "code_hash": "1ebf728c65b7d2752cdba00b790b5652",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Below is an example of code before the function was implemented - below we are establishing a connection to 2 different databases and it is obvious why this is such a strong case to implement a function!</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">db_name</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"test\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">load_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">find_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"C:/Users/</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getlogin</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">/.Renviron\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">connection_args</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Driver={Oracle in OraClient19Home1};\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DBQ=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_path'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DATABASE=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_schema'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"UID=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_username'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"PWD=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_password'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"s2\">\"Trusted_Connection=no;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"s2\">\"Port=1433\"</span>\n<span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">connection_string</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"se\">\\\"</span><span class=\"s2\">.join(connection_args)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">connection</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">pyodbc</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">connect</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">connection_string</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">db_name_prod</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"production\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">connection_args_production</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Driver={Oracle in OraClient19Home1};\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DBQ=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name_prod</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_path'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DATABASE=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name_prod</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_schema'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"UID=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name_prod</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_username'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"PWD=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name_prod</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_password'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"s2\">\"Trusted_Connection=no;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                   <span class=\"s2\">\"Port=1433\"</span>\n<span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">connection_string_prod</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"se\">\\\"</span><span class=\"s2\">.join(connection_args_production)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">connection_prod</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">pyodbc</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">connect</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">connection_string_prod</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
