    {
      "id": "ZHCJ",
      "code_hash": "5d04e4d18480b9543e7bdd8de37dbc53",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">By adding this function one could get the connection the the database by just calling:</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">test_connection</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">connect_db</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"test\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">prod_connection</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">connect_db</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"test\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ROlb",
      "code_hash": "efb4ccf3654cf13c7acec2b716c90183",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"pending-on-functions\">Pending on Functions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Defining inputs &amp; outputs</li>\n<li>Functions should do one thing and do them well!</li>\n<li>Functions should assume no existing state - the only thing that matters is the input to the function</li>\n<li>Other examples of cases to write functions for - add charts!</li>\n<li>Why a function for do_analysis() is not scaleable!</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "qnkX",
      "code_hash": "9126a473d57a1a53ea7d67163fdb3c62",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"testing\">Testing</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Go over what testing is - while building on the database connection example</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "TqIu",
      "code_hash": "35dea9d883fdd20e6fd5cb5d7e2e2bb5",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"in-code-exception-handling\">In-Code Exception Handling</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Writing functions in such a way does not just reduce redundancies it also helps consolidate processes and a well written function can catch an input errors upfront. And adding useful <code>try</code> <code>except</code> statements in our function we can easily avoid some expected mistakes.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Going back to the earlier example if I know that we only have 3 available databases namely <strong>test, prod, &amp; staging</strong> I can add this to my code:</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">db_name</span> <span class=\"ow\">not</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"test\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"prod\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"staging\"</span><span class=\"p\">]:</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">raise</span> <span class=\"ne\">ValueError</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n            <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\"> is not a valid database that our team has access to!\"</span>\n            <span class=\"s2\">\"Try one of the following: 'test', 'staging', 'prod'\"</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This update would make our function look like this:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Vxnm",
      "code_hash": "c86c9ae812dcdfaacd54da3d1bdcc579",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">connect_db</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"test\"</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    This function takes in the name of the database and establishes a connection</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    with that database.</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    Input:</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    - db_name: (str) the name of the database to connect to</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    Returns:</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">    - A pyodbc.Connection object which we can use to query our database</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    \"\"\"</span>\n\n    <span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">db_name</span> <span class=\"ow\">not</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"test\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"prod\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"staging\"</span><span class=\"p\">]:</span>\n            <span class=\"k\">raise</span> <span class=\"ne\">ValueError</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n                <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\"> is not a valid database that our team has access to!\"</span>\n                <span class=\"s2\">\"Try one of the following: 'test', 'staging', 'prod'\"</span>\n            <span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n    <span class=\"n\">load_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">find_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"C:/Users/</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getlogin</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">/.Renviron\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n\n    <span class=\"n\">connection_args</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Driver={Oracle in OraClient19Home1};\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DBQ=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_path'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"DATABASE=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_schema'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"UID=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_username'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"PWD=</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">environ</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s1\">'</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">db_name</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s1\">_password'</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"s2\">\"Trusted_Connection=no;\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n                       <span class=\"s2\">\"Port=1433\"</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">]</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">connection_string</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">join</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">connection_args</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">pyodbc</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">connect</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">connection_string</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DnEU",
      "code_hash": "4d1c2497793a4af12daecec11c96d796",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Building functions in such a way makes sure that the same processes are being followed by everyone on the team and it also allows us to raise try/except errors that are useful - this comes in super handy for code that interactes with the database since the errors one encounters there are often not helpful.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
